Embedded React: AVX2 rows for the software backend's blends.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed file: backends/software/renderer_backend.c. Proposed
upstream as pull request #317.

copy_rect_cb (source-over of premultiplied pixels, with opaque and transparent
shortcuts), the translucent branch of fill_rect_cb and blend_rect_cb below full
alpha handle eight pixels per step when the compiler targets AVX2 (the PS5
target is znver2), with the same integer arithmetic as over_premul and div255,
so the output is bit-identical to the scalar loops, which remain the path for
other targets and for each row's last columns. A harness built for x86-64 that
runs both on 300 random fills, copies and blends found no differing pixel. On
the PS5 a 1920x1080 mixed-alpha copy takes 1.4 ms and a blend at 200/255
1.7 ms.

